e stonelike chest of the demon Hiraṇyakaśipu."],"isLong":false},{"text":["ito nṛsiṁhaḥ parato nṛsiṁho","yato yato yāmi tato nṛsiṁhaḥ","bahir nṛsiṁho hṛdaye nṛsiṁho","nṛsiṁham ādiṁ śaraṇaṁ prapadye"],"translation":["Lord Nṛsiṁha is here and also there. Wherever I go Lord Nṛsiṁha is there. He is in the heart and is outside as well. I surrender to Lord Nṛsiṁha, the origin of all things and the supreme refuge."],"isLong":false},{"subtitle":["Śrī Daśāvatār-stotram"],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["tava kara-kamala-vare nakham adbhuta-śṛṅgaṁ","    dalita-hiraṇyakaśipu-tanu-bhṛṅgam","keśava dhṛta-narahari-rūpa jaya jagadīśa hare"],"translation":["Oh Keśava! Oh Lord of the universe! Oh Lord Hari, who have assumed the form of half-man, half-lion! All glories to You! Just as one can easily crush a wasp between one’s fingernails, so in the same way the body of the wasplike demon Hiraṇyakaśipu has been ripped apart by the wonderful pointed nails on Your beautiful lotus hands."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Srila B.S. Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/goswami-maharaj-s-ri-nr-sim-ha","personSlug":"srila-b-s-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/namas-te-narasimhaya","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"},{"title":"Bhakti Lalita Devi","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bhakti-lalita-devi/bhakti-lalita-devi-sri-nrsimha-pranam-namas-te-narisimhaya","personSlug":"bhakti-lalita-devi"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en-2022/namas-te-narasimhaya/","description":"Śrī Nṛsiṁha Praṇām — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Jayadeva Goswāmī with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Śrī Nṛsiṁha Praṇām | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-2022","slug":"namas-te-narasimhaya"}}